# What to focus on

## Next PR: terminal output safety (FOLLOWUP_TASKS 11, 12, 13)

Branch: `fix/terminal-output`. The approval prompt is gohome's main guardrail. These three items are the remaining ways untrusted text (model output, file names, session titles) can show on screen differently from what it is.

1. **11 Bidi characters are not flagged.** U+202E and similar characters can reorder text in the approval prompt, so a command can look different from what runs ("Trojan Source").
   - Characters: U+061C, U+200E, U+200F, U+202A-U+202E, U+2066-U+2069.
   - `showControls` (`tui/sanitize.go`) writes them as `\u202e` and sets `found`, so the existing warning line shows.
   - `sanitizeText` removes them from timeline text.
   - `hasControlChar` (`guard/suggest.go`) treats them as control characters, so no whitelist pattern is suggested.
   - Tests: each function with a command that contains U+202E.
2. **12 Unknown-tool summaries are cut before control characters are escaped.** `rawToolArg` (`tui/chat.go`) falls back to `shortSummary` on the raw JSON, so the 60-column cut is measured on raw text and can split an escape sequence. Move the `shortSummary` call out of `rawToolArg` and into its callers, after `sanitizeText` (timeline) or `showControls` (approval prompt).
   - Test: an unknown tool whose input has an escape sequence near column 57. The summary is cut on the cleaned text.
3. **13 File names and session titles are not sanitized.** A cloned repo can contain a file name with an escape sequence, and it is printed raw in the file search list.
   - Apply `sanitizeText` to `r.Path` in `filesearch.go` (display only; the selected value stays the real path).
   - Apply it to the title in `listingToItem` (`session_browser.go`). Check whether the `/resume` picker uses the same function, and sanitize it there too if not.
   - Tests: a file search result and a session listing that contain ESC.

Then:
- Remove items 11, 12 and 13 from `docs/FOLLOWUP_TASKS.md`. Add a CHANGELOG Unreleased entry.
- Each fix gets a failing test first. Run `go vet`, `go test`, `golangci-lint`. Update snapshots only if output changes on purpose.
- Live test with the gohome-full-test skill. In the TUI scratch dir, create a file whose name contains an escape sequence, open file search, and check with `capture-pane` that it shows no raw escape. Try an approval prompt with a command that contains U+202E. If the model removes the character (as it did with ESC for item 19), note it as tested by unit tests only.

Out of scope: other FOLLOWUP_TASKS items.
